/-!
# Idele classes are norms from an extension that splits almost everywhere

Let `L/K` be an extension of number fields and `S` a finite set of finite places of `K`. If at
every finite place `v ∉ S` every unit of `K_v` is a norm from `K_v ⊗[K] L`, then every idele class
of `K` is a norm from `L`: the norm map `C_L → C_K` is surjective
(`ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_range_normUnits_eq_top`). This holds in particular when
every finite place outside `S` has a place of `L` above it with local degree one, for instance
when it splits completely in `L` (`ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_finrank_eq_one`).

The proof is weak approximation. Every idele becomes, after multiplication by a principal idele,
an `n`-th power at the places of `S` and at every infinite place, for any `n ≠ 0`
(`exists_unitEmbedding_mul_mem_range_powMonoidHom`): the `n`-th powers of `K_v` contain the units
congruent to one to a sufficient level, a positive real number is an `n`-th power, and every
complex number is one. With `n = [L : K]` such a coordinate is the norm of its `n`-th root, and the
placewise norm criterion `mem_range_ideleNormMap_iff` assembles the local norms into an idele.

This is the norm half of Milne's Proposition 4.6, proved directly rather than through the density
of `K^× · I^S` in `I_K`. Together with the first fundamental inequality
`[C_K : N_{L/K} C_L] ≥ [L : K]` for cyclic `L/K`, it shows that a nontrivial solvable extension has
infinitely many places that do not split completely. That is how the Frobenius elements of an
abelian extension are seen to generate its Galois group without the Chebotarev density theorem, as
the Kummer-theoretic proof of the second fundamental inequality requires.

The fixed-field theorems are the norm half of Milne's Proposition 4.7, the step where the Frobenius
elements enter. Let `L/K` be Galois and `H` a subgroup of `Gal(L/K)`, with fixed field `E = L ^ H`.
If every finite place `v ∉ S` has a place `w` of `L` above it whose decomposition group `D(w)` lies
in `H`, then the place of `E` below `w` has local degree `[D(w) : D(w) ∩ H] = 1` over `v`
(`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.finrank_adicCompletion_fixedField`), so the norm map
`C_E → C_K` is surjective (`ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_stabilizer_le`).
A subgroup containing every Frobenius element at `w` contains `D(w)`, so this applies to the
subgroup generated by the Frobenius elements at the places outside `S`
(`ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_isArithFrobAt_mem`).

When `H` is normal and `Gal(L/K) ⧸ H` is solvable, a proper `H` lies in a normal subgroup of prime
index, whose fixed field is a cyclic extension of `K` of prime degree inside `E` with surjective
norm (`exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective`). The first inequality
`[C_K : N_{E/K}(C_E)] ≥ [E : K]` for cyclic `E/K` excludes such a field, so it forces `H = ⊤`.
Two cases are recorded. If `L/K` is solvable of degree greater than one and almost every place has
a place above it with trivial decomposition group, such a field exists
(`exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_stabilizer_eq_bot`): with the first
inequality this is Milne's Proposition 4.6. The subgroup generated by the Frobenius elements at
the places outside `S` is normal, since a conjugate of a Frobenius element at `w` is a Frobenius
element at a conjugate of `w`. So if `L/K` is solvable and these Frobenius elements do not generate
`Gal(L/K)`, such a field exists again
(`exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_closure_isArithFrobAt_ne_top`): with the
first inequality this is Milne's Proposition 4.7, that the Frobenius elements generate `Gal(L/K)`.

The same proof of the second fundamental inequality needs surjectivity in a second situation,
where the places outside `S` need not split (Milne's Proposition 6.10). Let `T` be a finite set of
finite places disjoint from `S`, where `S` generates the ideal class group, and let `[L : K]`
divide `n`. Suppose every element of `K_v` is a local norm at the places of `S` and at the infinite
places, `L` has an unramified place above every finite place outside `S ∪ T`, and the `S`-units
surject onto `∏_{v ∈ T} U_v / U_v ^ n`. Then `C_L → C_K` is again surjective
(`ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_mem_unit`). Here no approximation is used: an
idele class has a representative that is a unit outside `S`, and an `S`-unit corrects it to an
`n`-th power at `T` while preserving the unit condition outside `S`. The class group and `S`-unit
conditions concern `S` and `T` alone (the latter is Milne's Lemma 6.9). The local conditions hold
for a Kummer extension `L = K(b^{1/n})` of a field containing the `n`-th roots of unity when `b`
is an `n`-th power at `S` and at the infinite places, `b` is a unit outside `S ∪ T`, and `n` is a
unit outside `S`. The first inequality, applied to the cyclic extension `L/K`, then forces
`L = K`, so `b` is an `n`-th power: this is Milne's Proposition 6.10, from which his Lemma 6.7
computes the index of the Kummer idele subgroup in the proof of the second inequality.

## Main results

* `NumberField.InfinitePlace.Completion.mem_range_powMonoidHom`: a unit of an archimedean
  completion that is positive at a real place is an `n`-th power.
* `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.exists_unitEmbedding_mul_mem_range_powMonoidHom`: every idele is,
  up to a principal idele, an `n`-th power at the places of `S` and at the infinite places.
* `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.range_normUnits_adicCompletion_eq_top_of_finrank_eq_one`: every unit
  of `K_v` is a local norm when some place above `v` has local degree one.
* `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_range_normUnits_eq_top` and
  `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_finrank_eq_one`: the
  surjectivity of the idele-class norm map.
* `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_stabilizer_le` and
  `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_isArithFrobAt_mem`:
  the norm map from the fixed field of a subgroup containing the decomposition groups, or the
  Frobenius elements, at places above all but finitely many places of `K` is surjective.
* `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective`: if the
  decomposition groups at places above all but finitely many places of `K` lie in a proper normal
  subgroup `H` with solvable quotient, then `L ^ H` contains a Galois extension of `K` of prime
  degree with surjective idele-class norm map.
* `exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_stabilizer_eq_bot`: the same conclusion
  for a nontrivial solvable extension in which almost every place splits completely.
* `exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_closure_isArithFrobAt_ne_top`: the same
  conclusion for a solvable extension whose Frobenius elements outside `S` do not generate the
  Galois group.
* `TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_mem_unit`:
  surjectivity when the `S`-units surject onto the local power classes of units at `T`.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Class Field Theory*, v4.03, Chapter VII, Lemma 4.5, Proposition 4.6,
  Proposition 4.7 and Proposition 6.10.
-/

public section
noncomputable section

open IsDedekindDomain IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum NumberField NumberField.InfinitePlace
open scoped TensorProduct AdicCompletionExtension NumberField.LiesOver Pointwise

/-! ### `n`-th powers at an infinite place -/

namespace NumberField.InfinitePlace.Completion

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] {w : InfinitePlace K}

/-- **Units of an archimedean completion that are positive at a real place are `n`-th powers.**
At a real place this is the existence of real `n`-th roots of positive numbers; at a complex place
every unit is an `n`-th power. -/
theorem mem_range_powMonoidHom {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0) (y : w.Completionˣ)
    (hy : ∀ hw : w.IsReal, 0 < extensionEmbeddingOfIsReal hw y) :
    y ∈ (powMonoidHom n : w.Completionˣ →* w.Completionˣ).range := by
  by_cases hw : w.IsReal
  · let e := ringEquivRealOfIsReal hw
    have hpos : 0 < e y := by simpa [e] using hy hw
    -- The real `n`-th root `(e y) ^ (1 / n)` of the positive number `e y`.
    have ht0 : e.symm (e y ^ ((n : ℝ)⁻¹)) ≠ 0 :=
      (map_ne_zero e.symm).2 (Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hpos _).ne'
    refine ⟨Units.mk0 _ ht0, Units.ext ?_⟩
    rw [powMonoidHom_apply, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, Units.val_mk0, ← map_pow,
      Real.rpow_inv_natCast_pow hpos.le hn, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  · let e := ringEquivComplexOfIsComplex (not_isReal_iff_isComplex.mp hw)
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := IsAlgClosed.exists_pow_nat_eq (e y) (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hn)
    have hz0 : e.symm z ≠ 0 := by
      refine (map_ne_zero e.symm).2 fun h ↦ ?_
      rw [h, zero_pow hn] at hz
      exact (map_ne_zero e).2 y.ne_zero hz.symm
    refine ⟨Units.mk0 _ hz0, Units.ext ?_⟩
    rw [powMonoidHom_apply, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, Units.val_mk0, ← map_pow, hz,
      RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]

end NumberField.InfinitePlace.Completion

namespace TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields

/-! ### `n`-th powers at finitely many places -/

section Approximation

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K]

/-- **Every idele is an `n`-th power at finitely many places, up to a principal idele.** For a
finite set `S` of finite places and `n ≠ 0`, every idele times a suitable principal idele is an
`n`-th power at each place of `S` and at each infinite place. This is weak approximation at `S` and
the real places, through `exists_unitEmbedding_mul_mem_ideleCongrOneSubgroup` for a modulus deep
enough at `S` and divisible by every real place. -/
theorem exists_unitEmbedding_mul_mem_range_powMonoidHom (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0) (x : IdeleGroup (𝓞 K) K) :
    ∃ α : Kˣ,
      (∀ v ∈ S, v.ideleFiniteCoord (IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K α * x) ∈
        (powMonoidHom n : (v.adicCompletion K)ˣ →* (v.adicCompletion K)ˣ).range) ∧
      ∀ w : InfinitePlace K, w.ideleInfiniteCoord (IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K α * x) ∈
        (powMonoidHom n : w.Completionˣ →* w.Completionˣ).range := by
  -- At each finite place, the `n`-th powers contain the units congruent to one to a level `m v`.
  have hdeep (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) :
      ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ y : (v.adicCompletion K)ˣ, Valued.v (y : v.adicCompletion K) = 1 →
        Valued.v ((y : v.adicCompletion K) - 1) ≤ WithZero.exp (-(m : ℤ)) →
          y ∈ (powMonoidHom n : (v.adicCompletion K)ˣ →* (v.adicCompletion K)ˣ).range := by
    let _ : Finite (𝓞 K ⧸ v.asIdeal) := Ring.HasFiniteQuotients.finiteQuotient v.ne_bot
    obtain ⟨m, -, hm⟩ := TauCeti.hasBasis_nhds_one_unitFiltration.mem_iff.mp <|
      (TauCeti.isOpen_range_powMonoidHom
        ((Nat.cast_ne_zero (R := v.adicCompletion K)).2 hn)).mem_nhds (Subgroup.one_mem _)
    exact ⟨m, fun y hy1 hy ↦ hm ((mem_unitFiltration_adicCompletion_iff v).mpr ⟨hy1, hy⟩)⟩
  choose m hm using hdeep
  -- The modulus `∏_{v ∈ S} v ^ (m v + 1)`, divisible by every real place.
  let 𝔪 : Modulus K :=
    { finitePart := ∏ v ∈ S, v.asIdeal ^ (m v + 1)
      finitePart_ne_bot := by
        rw [← Ideal.zero_eq_bot, Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff]
        exact fun v _ ↦ pow_ne_zero _ (by simpa using v.ne_bot)
      infinitePart := (narrowModulus K).infinitePart }
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := exists_unitEmbedding_mul_mem_ideleCongrOneSubgroup 𝔪 x
  obtain ⟨hfin, hinf⟩ := mem_ideleCongrOneSubgroup_iff.mp hα
  refine ⟨α, fun v hv ↦ ?_, fun w ↦ ?_⟩
  · have hpow : v.asIdeal ^ (m v + 1) ∣ 𝔪.finitePart := Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem _ hv
    have hdvd : v.asIdeal ∣ 𝔪.finitePart := (dvd_pow_self _ (Nat.succ_ne_zero _)).trans hpow
    have hexp : m v + 1 ≤ 𝔪.exponent v :=
      (Modulus.pow_dvd_finitePart_iff_le_exponent 𝔪 v).mp hpow
    refine hm v _ (𝔪.valued_eq_one_of_valued_sub_one_le hdvd (hfin v hdvd))
      ((hfin v hdvd).trans (WithZero.exp_le_exp.mpr ?_))
    omega
  · exact Completion.mem_range_powMonoidHom hn _ fun hw ↦
      hinf ⟨w, hw⟩ (mem_narrowModulus_infinitePart ⟨w, hw⟩)

end Approximation

/-! ### Surjectivity of the idele-class norm map -/

variable {K L : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L] [NumberField L] [Algebra K L]

variable (L) in
/-- **Every unit of `K_v` is a local norm when some place above `v` has local degree one.** The
norm from `K_v ⊗[K] L` is then onto, the factor `L_w = K_v` alone providing every unit. -/
theorem range_normUnits_adicCompletion_eq_top_of_finrank_eq_one (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K))
    (w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal})
    (hw : Module.finrank (v.adicCompletion K) (w.1.adicCompletion L) = 1) :
    (Algebra.normUnits (v.adicCompletion K) (S := v.adicCompletion K ⊗[K] L)).range = ⊤ := by
  classical
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun a _ ↦ (mem_range_normUnits_adicCompletion_iff K L v a).mpr ?_
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Algebra.pow_finrank_mem_range_normUnits (v.adicCompletion K)
    (S := w.1.adicCompletion L) a
  refine ⟨Pi.mulSingle w b, ?_⟩
  rw [finprod_eq_single _ w fun w' hw' ↦ by rw [Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne hw', map_one],
    Pi.mulSingle_eq_same, hb, hw, pow_one]

/-- **The idele-class norm map is onto when local norms are onto outside finitely many places.**
If, at every finite place `v` of `K` outside a finite set `S`, every unit of `K_v` is a norm from
`K_v ⊗[K] L`, then every idele class of `K` is the norm of an idele class of `L`. -/
theorem ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_range_normUnits_eq_top
    (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hS : ∀ v ∉ S,
      (Algebra.normUnits (v.adicCompletion K) (S := v.adicCompletion K ⊗[K] L)).range = ⊤) :
    Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K L) := by
  classical
  intro c
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := QuotientGroup.mk_surjective c
  obtain ⟨α, hfin, hinf⟩ := exists_unitEmbedding_mul_mem_range_powMonoidHom S
    (Module.finrank_pos (R := K) (M := L)).ne' x
  -- A `[L : K]`-th power of a local unit is a local norm.
  have hpow {F : Type _} [Field F] [Algebra K F] {y : Fˣ}
      (hy : y ∈ (powMonoidHom (Module.finrank K L) : Fˣ →* Fˣ).range) :
      y ∈ (Algebra.normUnits F (S := F ⊗[K] L)).range :=
    Algebra.range_powMonoidHom_le_range_normUnits F (by rw [Module.finrank_baseChange]) hy
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (mem_range_ideleNormMap_iff K L _).mpr
    ⟨fun v ↦ if hv : v ∈ S then hpow (hfin v hv) else by simp [hS v hv],
      fun w ↦ hpow (hinf w)⟩
  refine ⟨(z : IdeleClassGroup (𝓞 L) L), ?_⟩
  rw [ContinuousMonoidHom.coe_toMonoidHom] at hz
  have hα : IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K α ∈ IdeleGroup.principalSubgroup (𝓞 K) K :=
    ⟨α, rfl⟩
  rw [ideleClassNormMap_mk, ← QuotientGroup.mk_mul_of_mem x hα, mul_comm]
  exact congrArg _ hz

/-- **Every idele class is a norm from an extension that splits almost everywhere.** If every
finite place `v` of `K` outside a finite set `S` has a place `w` of `L` above it with
`[L_w : K_v] = 1`, for instance because `v` splits completely in `L`, then the norm map
`C_L → C_K` is surjective. -/
theorem ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_finrank_eq_one
    (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hS : ∀ v ∉ S, ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
      Module.finrank (v.adicCompletion K) (w.1.adicCompletion L) = 1) :
    Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K L) :=
  ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_range_normUnits_eq_top S fun v hv ↦
    (hS v hv).elim (range_normUnits_adicCompletion_eq_top_of_finrank_eq_one L v)

/-- **Idele classes are norms from the fixed field of a group containing decomposition groups.**
Let `L/K` be Galois and `H` a subgroup of `Gal(L/K)`. If every finite place `v` of `K` outside a
finite set `S` has a place `w` of `L` above it whose decomposition group lies in `H`, then every
idele class of `K` is a norm from the fixed field `L ^ H`: the place of `L ^ H` below `w` has local
degree one over `v`. -/
theorem ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_stabilizer_le [IsGalois K L]
    (H : Subgroup (L ≃ₐ[K] L)) (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hS : ∀ v ∉ S, ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
      MulAction.stabilizer (L ≃ₐ[K] L) w.1.asIdeal ≤ H) :
    Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K (IntermediateField.fixedField H)) := by
  refine ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_finrank_eq_one S fun v hv ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨⟨w, _⟩, hle⟩ := hS v hv
  -- the place `u` of `L ^ H` below `w`
  let u := w.under (𝓞 (IntermediateField.fixedField H))
  have : w.asIdeal.LiesOver u.asIdeal := ⟨HeightOneSpectrum.under_asIdeal _ w⟩
  have hu : u.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal := by
    rw [HeightOneSpectrum.under_asIdeal]
    infer_instance
  exact ⟨⟨u, hu⟩, (finrank_adicCompletion_fixedField_eq_one_iff v w H u).mpr hle⟩

/-- **Idele classes are norms from the fixed field of a group containing Frobenius elements.** Let
`L/K` be Galois and `H` a subgroup of `Gal(L/K)`. If every finite place `v` of `K` outside a finite
set `S` has a place `w` of `L` above it such that `H` contains every arithmetic Frobenius element
at `w`, then every idele class of `K` is a norm from the fixed field `L ^ H`. At a place unramified
in `L` the Frobenius element is unique, so this is the case of the subgroup generated by the
Frobenius elements at the places of `L` outside `S`, once `S` contains the ramified places. -/
theorem ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_isArithFrobAt_mem [IsGalois K L]
    (H : Subgroup (L ≃ₐ[K] L)) (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hS : ∀ v ∉ S, ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
      ∀ σ : L ≃ₐ[K] L, IsArithFrobAt (𝓞 K) σ w.1.asIdeal → σ ∈ H) :
    Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K (IntermediateField.fixedField H)) :=
  ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_stabilizer_le H S fun v hv ↦
    (hS v hv).imp fun w hw ↦
      Ideal.stabilizer_le_of_forall_isArithFrobAt_mem w.1.asIdeal w.1.ne_bot hw

/-- **Every idele class is a norm when `S`-units control the local power classes at `T`**
(Milne, *Class Field Theory*, VII, Proposition 6.10). Let `S` and `T` be disjoint finite sets of
finite places of `K`, with the classes of the primes of `S` generating the ideal class group, and
let `[L : K]` divide `n`. Suppose that

* at the places of `S` and at the infinite places every element of `K_v` is a local norm,
* at every finite place outside `S ∪ T` some place of `L` above it is unramified, and
* the `S`-units surject onto `∏_{v ∈ T} U_v / U_v ^ n`: every family of local units at `T` agrees
  with a single `S`-unit up to local `n`-th powers.

Then the norm map `C_L → C_K` is surjective. -/
theorem ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_forall_exists_mem_unit
    (S T : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K))) (hST : Disjoint S T) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : Module.finrank K L ∣ n)
    (hcl : Subgroup.closure
      (HeightOneSpectrum.classGroupMk '' (S : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))) = ⊤)
    (hS : ∀ v ∈ S,
      (Algebra.normUnits (v.adicCompletion K) (S := v.adicCompletion K ⊗[K] L)).range = ⊤)
    (hinf : ∀ w : InfinitePlace K,
      (Algebra.normUnits w.Completion (S := w.Completion ⊗[K] L)).range = ⊤)
    (hunr : ∀ v ∉ S, v ∉ T →
      ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
        Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt (𝓞 K) w.1.asIdeal)
    (hT : ∀ y : (v : T) → (v.1.adicCompletion K)ˣ,
      (∀ v, Valued.v (y v : v.1.adicCompletion K) = 1) →
      ∃ u ∈ (S : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K))).unit K, ∀ v : T,
        (Units.map (algebraMap K (v.1.adicCompletion K)).toMonoidHom u)⁻¹ * y v ∈
          (powMonoidHom n).range) :
    Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K L) := by
  classical
  intro c
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := QuotientGroup.mk_surjective c
  -- A representative `x * a` of the class that is a unit at every finite place outside `S`.
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := IdeleGroup.exists_valued_ideleFiniteCoord_mul_unitEmbedding_eq_one hcl x
  set x' := x * IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K a with hx'
  obtain ⟨u, huS, hu⟩ := hT (fun v ↦ v.1.ideleFiniteCoord x')
    fun v ↦ ha v.1 fun hv ↦ Finset.disjoint_left.mp hST hv v.2
  have hu' := (IdeleGroup.forall_valued_ideleFiniteCoord_unitEmbedding_eq_one_iff
    (R := 𝓞 K) (T := (S : Set (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))) u).mpr huS
  set z := x' * IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K u⁻¹ with hz
  have hzcoord (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) : v.ideleFiniteCoord z =
      (Units.map (algebraMap K (v.adicCompletion K)).toMonoidHom u)⁻¹ * v.ideleFiniteCoord x' := by
    rw [map_mul, mul_comm, map_inv, map_inv, ideleFiniteCoord_unitEmbedding]
  -- An `n`-th power of a local unit is a local norm, since `[L : K]` divides `n`.
  have hpow {F : Type _} [Field F] [Algebra K F] {y : Fˣ}
      (hy : y ∈ (powMonoidHom n : Fˣ →* Fˣ).range) :
      y ∈ (Algebra.normUnits F (S := F ⊗[K] L)).range :=
    Algebra.range_powMonoidHom_le_range_normUnits F (by rwa [Module.finrank_baseChange]) hy
  have hfin (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) : v.ideleFiniteCoord z ∈
      (Algebra.normUnits (v.adicCompletion K) (S := v.adicCompletion K ⊗[K] L)).range := by
    by_cases hvS : v ∈ S
    · simp [hS v hvS]
    by_cases hvT : v ∈ T
    · rw [hzcoord]
      exact hpow (hu ⟨v, hvT⟩)
    -- Outside `S ∪ T` the coordinate is a unit, and units are norms from an unramified place.
    have hval : Valued.v (v.ideleFiniteCoord z : v.adicCompletion K) = 1 := by
      rw [hzcoord, Units.val_mul, map_mul, ha v hvS, mul_one]
      simpa using hu' v hvS
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_unit_preimages_of_isUnramifiedAt K L v _ hval (hunr v hvS hvT)
    exact (mem_range_normUnits_adicCompletion_iff K L v _).mpr ⟨w, hw.1⟩
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (mem_range_ideleNormMap_iff K L z).mpr ⟨hfin, fun w ↦ by simp [hinf w]⟩
  refine ⟨(y : IdeleClassGroup (𝓞 L) L), ?_⟩
  replace hy : ideleNormMap K L y = z := hy
  have hmem : IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K a * IdeleGroup.unitEmbedding (𝓞 K) K u⁻¹ ∈
      IdeleGroup.principalSubgroup (𝓞 K) K := ⟨a * u⁻¹, map_mul _ _ _⟩
  rw [ideleClassNormMap_mk, hy, hz, hx', mul_assoc]
  exact QuotientGroup.mk_mul_of_mem x hmem

/-! ### Prime-degree subextensions with surjective norm -/

/-- **A solvable extension above the decomposition groups contains a prime-degree subextension from
which every idele class is a norm.** Let `L/K` be Galois and `H` a proper normal subgroup of
`Gal(L/K)` with solvable quotient. If every finite place `v` of `K` outside a finite set `S` has a
place `w` of `L` above it whose decomposition group lies in `H`, then the fixed field `L ^ H`
contains a Galois extension `E/K` of prime degree, hence cyclic, with `N_{E/K}(C_E) = C_K`.

The first fundamental inequality `[C_K : N_{E/K}(C_E)] ≥ [E : K]` for cyclic `E/K` rules out such
an `E`, and so rules out such an `H`. -/
theorem exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective [IsGalois K L]
    (H : Subgroup (L ≃ₐ[K] L)) [H.Normal] [Group.IsSolvable ((L ≃ₐ[K] L) ⧸ H)] (hH : H ≠ ⊤)
    (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hS : ∀ v ∉ S, ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
      MulAction.stabilizer (L ≃ₐ[K] L) w.1.asIdeal ≤ H) :
    ∃ E : IntermediateField K L, E ≤ IntermediateField.fixedField H ∧ IsGalois K E ∧
      (Module.finrank K E).Prime ∧ Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K E) := by
  -- The fixed field of a normal subgroup `B ⊇ H` of prime index.
  obtain ⟨B, hB, hHB, hp⟩ := H.exists_normal_le_index_prime hH
  refine ⟨IntermediateField.fixedField B, IntermediateField.fixedField_le hHB, inferInstance, ?_,
    ideleClassNormMap_fixedField_surjective_of_stabilizer_le B S fun v hv ↦
      (hS v hv).imp fun _ h ↦ h.trans hHB⟩
  rwa [IntermediateField.finrank_eq_fixingSubgroup_index,
    IntermediateField.fixingSubgroup_fixedField]

/-- **A nontrivial solvable extension in which almost every place splits completely contains a
prime-degree subextension from which every idele class is a norm.** Let `L/K` be a Galois extension
of degree greater than one with solvable Galois group. If every finite place `v` of `K` outside a
finite set `S` has a place `w` of `L` above it with trivial decomposition group, then `L` contains
a Galois extension `E/K` of prime degree, hence cyclic, with `N_{E/K}(C_E) = C_K`.

The first fundamental inequality for cyclic extensions rules out such an `E`, and so shows that a
nontrivial solvable extension has infinitely many places that do not split completely. -/
theorem exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_stabilizer_eq_bot [IsGalois K L]
    [Group.IsSolvable (L ≃ₐ[K] L)] (hL : 1 < Module.finrank K L)
    (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hS : ∀ v ∉ S, ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
      MulAction.stabilizer (L ≃ₐ[K] L) w.1.asIdeal = ⊥) :
    ∃ E : IntermediateField K L, IsGalois K E ∧ (Module.finrank K E).Prime ∧
      Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K E) := by
  have hbot : (⊥ : Subgroup (L ≃ₐ[K] L)) ≠ ⊤ := by
    rw [ne_eq, eq_comm, Subgroup.eq_bot_iff_card, Subgroup.card_top, IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank]
    exact hL.ne'
  obtain ⟨E, -, hE⟩ := exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective ⊥ hbot S
    fun v hv ↦ (hS v hv).imp fun _ h ↦ h.le
  exact ⟨E, hE⟩

/-- **The Frobenius elements outside `S` generate a solvable Galois group, unless a prime-degree
subextension has surjective norm.** Let `L/K` be Galois with solvable Galois group, and `S` a
finite set of finite places of `K`. If the arithmetic Frobenius elements at the places of `L` above
the finite places of `K` outside `S` do not generate `Gal(L/K)`, then `L` contains a Galois
extension `E/K` of prime degree, hence cyclic, with `N_{E/K}(C_E) = C_K`.

The subgroup they generate is normal, since a conjugate of a Frobenius element at `w` is a
Frobenius element at a conjugate of `w`. The first fundamental inequality for cyclic extensions
rules out such an `E`, and so shows that the Frobenius elements generate `Gal(L/K)`. -/
theorem exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective_of_closure_isArithFrobAt_ne_top
    [IsGalois K L] [Group.IsSolvable (L ≃ₐ[K] L)] (S : Finset (HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)))
    (hgen : Subgroup.closure {σ : L ≃ₐ[K] L | ∃ v ∉ S,
      ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
        IsArithFrobAt (𝓞 K) σ w.1.asIdeal} ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ E : IntermediateField K L, IsGalois K E ∧ (Module.finrank K E).Prime ∧
      Function.Surjective (ideleClassNormMap K E) := by
  set X : Set (L ≃ₐ[K] L) := {σ | ∃ v ∉ S,
    ∃ w : {w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 L) // w.asIdeal.LiesOver v.asIdeal},
      IsArithFrobAt (𝓞 K) σ w.1.asIdeal}
  have : (Subgroup.closure X).Normal := by
    refine Subgroup.closure_normal_of_forall_conj_mem fun τ σ ⟨v, hv, w, hσ⟩ ↦ ?_
    -- `τ σ τ⁻¹` is a Frobenius element at the place `τ • w`, which again lies over `v`.
    let w' := (liesOverEquivPrimesOver (𝓞 L) v).symm (τ • liesOverEquivPrimesOver (𝓞 L) v w)
    have hw' : w'.1.asIdeal = τ • w.1.asIdeal := by
      simp [w', coe_smul_primesOver_ringOfIntegers]
    exact ⟨v, hv, w', hw' ▸ hσ.conj τ⟩
  obtain ⟨E, -, hE⟩ := exists_finrank_prime_ideleClassNormMap_surjective (Subgroup.closure X) hgen S
    fun v hv ↦ by
      obtain ⟨Q⟩ := v.asIdeal.nonempty_primesOver (S := 𝓞 L)
      let w := (liesOverEquivPrimesOver (𝓞 L) v).symm Q
      exact ⟨w, Ideal.stabilizer_le_of_forall_isArithFrobAt_mem w.1.asIdeal w.1.ne_bot
        fun σ hσ ↦ Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨v, hv, w, hσ⟩⟩
  exact ⟨E, hE⟩

end TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields
